{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "31", "m": "07", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "05", "M": "22", "S": "15"}}, "news": [{"title": "New Noida land acquisition begins in August, 40% area earmarked for industries", "para": "Noida Authority begins land acquisition for New Noida in August.  Lekhpals will survey 37 villages for the initial phase.  The project aims to ease urbanisation pressure and boost economic activity.  Infrastructure development will follow land acquisition and plot allotment.  New Noida is planned as a smart city and industrial hub.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/new-noida-land-acquisition-40-of-area-designated-for-industries/132754669?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-2098532/132754669.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Andhra Pradesh did not seek PMAY-U 2.0 houses for Amaravati: Centre", "para": "The Union government informed Parliament that Andhra Pradesh did not request housing under PMAY-U 2.0 for Amaravati.  The state submitted proposals for other urban local bodies, receiving approval for many houses.  Central assistance has been released for sanctioned houses, exceeding the maximum eligibility.  The original PMAY-U scheme in Andhra Pradesh is extended for completing sanctioned houses.  Eligible beneficiaries in Amaravati need coverage under the housing scheme.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/andhra-pradesh-government-fails-to-request-pmay-u-20-housing-for-amaravati-says-centre/132754485?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-128085/132754485.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "West Bengal mandates wastewater recycle in housing societies", "para": "West Bengal has issued a policy for safe treated wastewater reuse. Residential units must reuse treated wastewater for non-potable purposes. Industrial water needs will see 20% wastewater use by 2030. A GIS platform will manage water demand and wastewater generation. Urban local bodies will develop water resource management plans.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/west-bengal-introduces-mandatory-wastewater-recycle-policy-for-housing-societies/132754402?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-1510129/132754402.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}